# WINDOW (= PLOCATE: the pixel array fixed in detector coordinates) then PIXEL, and GBS beam sizes written to
# beamSize.txt in the working directory (hence cd $TMP; the deck is a COPY) on the manual's Cassegrain
# (cmdref: Window & Post-Processing / Ray Tracing).  GBS: 4 m at the source, 3.99 m on the primary, 0.997 m
# on the secondary, 2.1e-10 at the focus.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
cd $TMP
old $DECK
none
window
tout
2e-6
0,0
0,0
pix 5
64
2e-6
gbs
0
5
! cat $TMP/beamSize.txt
# EXPECT: Enter pixel size for placing window: \[0\.00000\]: 2e-6\s+Enter pixel coords of element vertex \(x,y\): \[0\.00000,0\.00000\]: 0,0\s+Enter window location in pixel coords \(x,y\): \[0\.00000,0\.00000\]: 0,0
# EXPECT: Peak intensity= 8\.8773143D\+06
# EXPECT: iElt =\s+0, Source aperture =\s+4\.0000
# EXPECT: Result is saved in file beamSize\.txt
# EXPECT: iElt =\s+2 \(Primary\s*, Reflector\s*\)\s+Beam diameter =\s+3\.9911950913D\+00
# EXPECT: iElt =\s+3 \(Secondary\s*, Reflector\s*\)\s+Beam diameter =\s+9\.9735754537D-01
# EXPECT: iElt =\s+5 \(Detector\s*, FocalPlane\s*\)\s+Beam diameter =\s+2\.14310100\d+D-10
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
